.TH quotadial-alerts 1  "QuotaDial 0.3.0" QuotaDial
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
quotadial\-alerts \- List the alert rules and what they told lately, or add, remove, or turn one on or off. Rules are written in plain words, such as `quotadial alerts add "warn me at 80%"`
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBquotadial alerts\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the alert rules and what they told lately, or add, remove, or turn one on or off. Rules are written in plain words, such as `quotadial alerts add "warn me at 80%"`
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
quotadial\-alerts\-list(1)
List the rules and what they told in the last week. The default
.TP
quotadial\-alerts\-add(1)
Add a rule written in plain words, such as "warn me at 80%", "warn me when the weekly window will run out before it resets" or "tell me 30 minutes before the session resets if it is above 50%"
.TP
quotadial\-alerts\-remove(1)
Remove the rule with this number
.TP
quotadial\-alerts\-on(1)
Turn the rule with this number on
.TP
quotadial\-alerts\-off(1)
Turn the rule with this number off
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
quotadial(1). The full guide is docs/CLI.md in QuotaDial\*(Aqs repository, https://github.com/pghmatt/quotadial, and quotadial.com.
